Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: keep the damage clips on a flip unless the buffer is dumb

Since "drm/virtio: Disable damage clipping if FB changed since last
page-flip" the driver flushes the whole plane whenever the framebuffer
changes, because uploads are done per buffer.  A compositor flips to
another buffer of its swapchain every frame, so every flush covers the
whole screen, although the commit's damage clips say what changed.

A blob - a native context's buffer, or guest memory the host maps
itself - is not uploaded: the host renders into it or reads it directly.  For it the clips only tell the host
which part of the screen changed since the previous frame, whichever
buffer that was in, and a host that copies the scanout into buffers of its
own (QEMU's SDL window with its own swapchain) can copy just that instead
of a whole 4K frame per refresh.

Only dumb buffers are uploaded per buffer: keep the clips for every other
framebuffer; a dumb one still flushes the whole plane on a flip.  The flag
is now decided for every commit: a duplicated plane state inherits it, so
once set (at the first flip after boot) it stayed set for good.  Module parameter blob_damage=0 restores the full
flushes.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -40,6 +40,11 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(flush_unchanged, "Flush the scanout on commits that leave it unchanged (default 0)");
 module_param_named(flush_unchanged, virtio_gpu_modparam_flush_unchanged, int, 0644);
 
+/* blob_damage=0 flushes the whole plane again whenever a framebuffer is flipped in */
+static int virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_damage = 1;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(blob_damage, "Keep the damage clips when a framebuffer that is not a dumb buffer is flipped in (default 1)");
+module_param_named(blob_damage, virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_damage, int, 0644);
+
 static const uint32_t virtio_gpu_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_XRGB8888,
 };
@@ -120,9 +125,20 @@
 	 * Ignore damage clips if the framebuffer attached to the plane's state
 	 * has changed since the last plane update (page-flip). In this case, a
 	 * full plane update should happen because uploads are done per-buffer.
+	 *
+	 * Only dumb buffers are uploaded: the host renders into the others or reads the guest's
+	 * memory itself, so the clips only tell the host which part of the
+	 * screen changed since the previous frame, whichever buffer that was in
+	 * - the damage of the atomic commit.  A host that copies the scanout
+	 * into its own buffers can then copy just that.
+	 *
+	 * The flag is decided anew for every commit: a duplicated plane state
+	 * inherits it, and once set it would stay set.
 	 */
-	if (old_plane_state->fb != new_plane_state->fb)
-		new_plane_state->ignore_damage_clips = true;
+	new_plane_state->ignore_damage_clips =
+		old_plane_state->fb != new_plane_state->fb &&
+		!(virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_damage &&
+		  !gem_to_virtio_gpu_obj(new_plane_state->fb->obj[0])->dumb);
 
 	crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(state,
 					       new_plane_state->crtc);
